  "Edward Jonas, publisher of the Henderson Journal, led the campaign, and the library opened on August 1, 1904, built of white limestone with tall classical columns. Downstairs was remodelled in 1960, an addition came in 1979 and 1980, and from 2002 to 2004 the rotunda murals, copper roof, stained-glass skylight, chandelier, doors and mosaic floor were restored. It is still the county library.",
