  "Professor B. F. Gabby, principal of Hickman College, led the effort with the school board; the college gave the lot and Captain H. A. Tylar gave $1,000 for books. The one-storey brick Colonial Revival library by Whitfield & King was finished in October 1908. It stood empty after a new library opened in 1975, and in 1989 it was being made into a museum and tourist centre. On the National Register since 1990. Its present use was not checked.",
