  "The library has been in the town since 1914 and stood empty after the public library moved out in 1977. A group formed to restore it, Hopkinsville Carnegie Library, Inc., plans a library of Kentucky architecture with tutoring, lectures, a gallery and a recital hall; in 2018 the work was about two-thirds done.",
